  "summary": "pypdf: Possible large memory usage when retrieving Roman page labels",
  "details": "### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory consumption. This requires accessing the page labels of a document with large Roman numerals.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.17.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.17.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4047](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4047).",
